{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":52134,"duration_api_ms":51858,"num_turns":16,"result":"I rewrote `CLAUDE.md` in place. I haven't built any lesson or run the CI smoke test, so the commands come from the Makefiles and workflows I read. The old version assumed every lesson uses libbpf and a Makefile, which isn't true.\n\n- **Two build styles:** Lessons 1–10 have no Makefile and build with `ecc` and `ecli`. Lessons 11+ use a libbpf Makefile. There are also a few special cases (`cargo` for Rust, Go for goroutine tracing, extra dependencies for CUDA and energy).\n- **Makefile details:** The `APPS=` line lists the binaries to build, and the build runs through `bpftool` and a generated skeleton. The vmlinux header is chosen by `ARCH`, and `V=1` shows full commands. I also listed the `make -C src` build-all and clean commands.\n- **Submodules:** The `bpftool` and `blazesym` submodules need `git submodule update --init --recursive` or builds fail.\n- **CI:** It builds each lesson and runs some for 3 seconds, treating exit code 124 as success.\n- **Writing lessons:** README files come in English and Chinese pairs. New lessons must be linked in the index files, and the style guides are in `src/scripts/`. `rename.py` hard-codes a `/root` path, so it shouldn't be run as-is.\n\nI dropped the old directory-range summary because it was partly wrong, such as listing lessons 0–10 as libbpf. I also removed \"Cilium eBPF\" and \"libbpf-rs\" from the overview because I found no code for them.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"26210ca1-6495-414d-a4a9-a5120f0ddda0","total_cost_usd":0.29469345,"usage":{"input_tokens":18,"cache_creation_input_tokens":32073,"cache_read_input_tokens":265119,"output_tokens":6322,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":32073},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_toke